{title: 196 - Tell Me the Old, Old Story}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #196 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 196}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Tell me the old, old [Eb]sto[Bb]ry, Of [Gm]unseen things [Fsus]above[F],
[F7]Of [Bb]Jesus and His [Eb]glory, Of [Bb]Jesus [F]and His [Bb]love;
[F]Tell me the [F7]story [Bb]simply, As [C]to a [C7]little [F]child
[F7]For [Bb]I am weak and [Eb]weary, And [Bb]helpless [F]and de[Bb]filed.
[Bb]Tell me the old, old [Eb]sto[Bb]ry, [F7]Tell me the old, old sto[Bb]ry,
[Bb]Tell me the old, [Bb7]old [Eb]story, Of [Bb]Jesus [F7]and His [Bb]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]Tell me [Eb]the old, [Bb]old story, [Gm]tell me [Fsus]the old, [F]old story,
[F7]Tell [Bb]me the [Eb]old, old [Bb]story, of [F]Jesus and [Bb]His love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Tell [Eb]me the [Bb]story softly, [Gm]with [Fsus]earnest tones [F]and grave;
[F7]Remember [Bb]I'm the [Eb]sinner [Bb]whom Jesus [F]came [Bb]to save.
[F]Tell [F7]me the [Bb]story always, [C]if [C7]you would [F]really be,
[F7]In [Bb]any time [Eb]of [Bb]trouble, a [F]comforter [Bb]to me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Tell me [Eb]the same [Bb]old story [Gm]when you [Fsus]have cause [F]to fear
[F7]That [Bb]this world's [Eb]empty glory [Bb]is [F]costing me [Bb]too dear.
[F]Yes, [F7]and when [Bb]that world's [C]glory is [C7]dawning on [F]my soul,
[F7]Tell [Bb]me the [Eb]old, old [Bb]story: "Christ [F]Jesus makes [Bb]thee whole."
{end_of_verse}
